# CRONTAB.SYS for the XRouter under test.
#
# Work-around for FINDINGS "XRouter broadcasts NODES only on its first
# port": with NODESINTERVAL=1 XRouter's scheduled NODES broadcasts only ever
# go out on port 1 (LinBPQ). XNet and TheNet learn their neighbours from
# NODES (XNet does not even open the link until it hears one), so without
# this the peer tests could not get started. BC <port> sends an immediate
# NODES broadcast on that port (MAN BCAST(1)); this does it every minute on
# the peer ports 3 to 6. Port 2 (LinBPQ3) is left alone on purpose so that
# test_xrouter_broadcasts_nodes_to_bpq3 still sees the bug.
#
# <min> <hour> <date> <month> <day> <command> [args]
* * * * * BC 3
* * * * * BC 4
* * * * * BC 5
* * * * * BC 6
